+# Screen / raster translation correspondence — r137
+
+## Task and authority
+
+This is PlusCal → JavaScript translation, not feature design. Read the complete development policy v0.2.6 again, complete renderer Source/PlusCal, public layout Source/PlusCal, interface FSM Source/PlusCal, Application adapter Source/PlusCal, system Source/PlusCal, Mantine Source and current plan. Ambiguous current-capture intent was checked directly against `sourcescript/frontend/renderer.py`, `renderDashboardCurrent`: supplied snapshot plus one-shot viewport is allowed, persistent target width/height must not change, and target limit/encoding/handoff/error/finally rules apply. No policy or upper-layer changes.
+
+## Stage 1: screen procedure and actual-caller map
+
+The following is a static translation-scope conclusion, **not** an executed fidelity/browser/checker pass.
+
+| PlusCal procedure in `pseudocode/frontend/renderer.pcal` | JavaScript realization and actual boundary |
+| --- | --- |
+| syncDashboardCaption | `sourcecode/frontend/renderer.js`: syncDashboardCaptionProjection; `sourcecode/application/adapter.js`: syncDashboardCaption supplies official caption input; public caption edits and Mantine editors use this boundary. Literal text/name/settings, visibility and supplied scaling; no project read inside renderer. |
+| publishUiTelemetry / setDebugEnabled / status | `sourcecode/frontend/renderer.js`: corresponding telemetry/debug/status functions; runtime status is one-way display, not project authority. |
+| applyDashboardProjectionInvalidation | `sourcecode/frontend/renderer.js`: same entry; `sourcecode/application/adapter.js`: applyCommittedDashboardProjection gates uncommitted results and supplies current official input/final runtime state. Label/image/palette/caption narrow branches preserve live surfaces; structural/source/geometry mismatch falls back to full supplied render. |
+| renderDashboard / CompleteGraphRender / CompleteImageRender | `sourcecode/frontend/renderer.js`: renderDashboardProjection, presentSuppliedGraph, current host/operation/generation checks and independent image surfaces. Supplied rows/columns/figure/image/labels/styles only. Empty/image/graph branches, removal, reuse, queued success/current failure/stale completion and detached/reparented children mapped. Existing resize queue retains requesting associations; native/fallback observer installation has one owner. |
+| setSelectedSlot / resolveSelectedChart / updateGraphView | `sourcecode/application/public_api/layout_annotations.js`: setSelectedSlot → dispatchSlotSelection → updateGraphView; `sourcecode/application/adapter.js` hands final supplied inputs to updateGraphViewProjection. `sourcecode/frontend/renderer.js`: resolveSelectedChart resolves only supplied relations. Rejection silent; same user target toggles; model selection retains; optional type command only for final non-null empty slot; no synthetic global resize. Mantine reads final public workspace/selection. |
+| installSlotClickController / HandleSlotClick | `sourcecode/frontend/renderer.js`: installSlotClickControllerProjection; bookmark selects content slots, empty surface selects empty slots, content body interaction does not select. Public actions own validation/mutation. |
+| StartBookmarkDrag / EndBookmarkDrag / ConsumePostDragClick / swapSlotContents | Same controller and suppression-token cleanup; current token owns one post-drag click or delayed no-click cleanup. Valid internal target invokes one public swap. OS-file drag is separate; no duplicate persistent commit at finish. |
+| finishDashboardFileDropInteraction / Renderer_prepareDashboardFileDrop | `sourcecode/frontend/renderer.js`: clearSlotDragState; `sourcecode/application/public_api/layout_annotations.js`: prepareDashboardFileDrop; `sourcecode/frontend/mantine_ui.js`: dashboardExternalFileDrop and mounted FastFigureDashboardFileDrop. Direct host target, public prepare-not-toggle, one awaited import/collision operation, finally drag-only finish. Stable mounted receiver does not depend on ordinary render-local state. |
+| applyUiPalette / applySlotStyle | `sourcecode/frontend/renderer.js`: applyUiPaletteProjection/applySlotStyleProjection/applyReferenceGeometryProjection; Application acquires supplied input. Actual Mantine style/grid/zoom/lock/reset calls use full supplied render for content and geometry; completion notification is not another render. |
+| startupCoreRuntime / readDashboardRenderedWidth | `sourcecode/frontend/renderer.js`: startupCoreRuntimeProjection and readDashboardRenderedWidth; `sourcecode/application/adapter.js`: initial official input/public action handoff; `sourcecode/system.js`: lifecycle ready and final owner-based audit. Startup order is zoom → controller → existing supplied slots → style → supplied reference audit. No default CSV/fake graph/grid recreation. Width is one finite positive measured scalar or none, never a project setting. |
+
+One additional untranslated primitive was found while completing this map: startup applied style but omitted `AuditSuppliedProjectReferenceRuntimeProjectionContracts`. r137 now realizes that primitive locally with `auditSuppliedRendererContracts`: unique visible slots, supplied chart/image relation identity, labels pointing into the supplied visible set, and runtime selected reference in that set. It neither queries Backend nor repairs/publishes input. The existing final system audit remains responsible for authoritative project invariants through their owners. It is not substituted for the earlier supplied-input audit.
+
+Stage 1 static translation scope is closed after this correction. Native Plotly, mounted listener timing, real pointer/browser rendering and inline/split verification remain pending; their absence is not treated as a translation permission gate. Historical OPEN notes remain historical rather than being deleted or silently rewritten.
